# PSR-4b-configure-3 — generated `/host/http` façade (partial)

## Problem proved before this wave

After PSR-4b-configure retargeted adapters to
`@app-tour/workspace-*/host/http`, `guard-api-workspace-isolation` failed on the
hand-written configure files: allowlist ceiling is **0**, and only `*.generated.ts`
may import `/host/*`.

SoT §PSR-4.4 still wants product-named configure deleted. Full deletion in one
wave would relocate ~400 lines of host port wiring into a generated body (or a
neutral builder + generated call sites) while also relocating Urban exposure
(branded symbols) without violating neutrality. That is **configure-3b**.

## Scope (this land)

| Work | Done |
| --- | --- |
| Inventory why isolation fails on configure | Yes |
| Add Urban `exposureHost` to manifest → exposure bindings | Yes |
| Add `productHttpHost` manifest + schema → HTTP host bindings | Yes |
| Generate `workspace-product-http-host-bindings.generated.ts` | Yes |
| Retarget denali/urban configure to import façade (not package `/host/http`) | Yes |
| Retarget Urban exposure imports via exposure generated bindings | Yes |
| Expire tsconfig bare `@app-tour/workspace-urban/exposure` alias | Yes |
| Delete product-named configure files | **No** → configure-3b |
| Move port wiring body into generated file | **No** → configure-3b |

Land commit: `7c61190d`

## Architecture (after this wave)

```text
app.ts
  → side-effect import configure-urban / configure-denali / configure-finance
configure-*-http-host.ts  (hand-written adapters; product-named count still 2)
  → import configure* + types from workspace-product-http-host-bindings.generated.ts
  → (urban) exposure symbols from workspace-exposure-host-bindings.generated.ts
*.generated.ts
  → only place with @app-tour/workspace-*/host/* imports
```

## Ratchet

| Check | Expect |
| --- | --- |
| `node scripts/ops/psr-4b-configure-smoke.mjs` | product-named **2**/2; configure files **3** |
| `node scripts/guards/guard-api-workspace-isolation.mjs` | **PASS** |
| `node scripts/ops/psr-4b-api-neutrality-smoke.mjs` | unapproved host-source **0** |

## Explicit non-goals

- Collapsing product-named ceiling to 0
- Changing finance configure (already platform-neutral)
- Harbor product HTTP host (none today)
